Package: zigimports
Type: Package
Title: Call 'Zig' Code from R
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Lakshya", "Sharma", email = "lakshya6115@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Amrit", "Pal", email = "amrit.pal@vit.ac.in", role = "aut"))
Description: Loads shared libraries compiled from 'Zig' ('.so' files on Linux,
    '.dll' files on Windows) and binds their exported functions to R
    functions. Arguments are passed by value using the native calling
    convention, so functions with mixed integer, double, logical, string and
    vector arguments and with return values can be called. Also compiles and
    runs 'Zig' code directly from R. Compiling code requires the 'Zig'
    compiler.
URL: https://github.com/lokop5116/zigimports
BugReports: https://github.com/lokop5116/zigimports/issues
License: GPL-3
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 3.5.0)
SystemRequirements: 'Zig' compiler (>= 0.11), only needed for zig_call()
    and to build libraries
Suggests: testthat (>= 3.0.0)
Config/testthat/edition: 3
RoxygenNote: 7.3.2
